Z||000000||cmyokley||01-13-2000||03:11 PM||||I have one problem with MY 86gt that is driving me crazy. It seems to be in the computer???? I can drive the car and everything will be fine for several miles then the idle will start going up and down then the car will die and not re-start. I can let it sit for five minutes and it will then re-start. I am about to go crazy over this one. Any ideas? The distributor is a new re-built one with a very new GM module, new coil, wires etc...etc.<P>Please Help.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Greg Piet||01-13-2000||03:56 PM||||I had a similar problem after putting in a reman dist.  I was aboutt o replace the computer, but i went back and gave a good lond look at teh reman dist.  Turned outthe dist was defective.  The base where the ign module sits was loose and free to rotate, but not the outer shaft when i secured it at the block, and the inner shaft had a bit of wobble.  I took it back to where I got it and screamed bloody murder.  Got another one and all was fixed. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||cmyokley||01-13-2000||05:15 PM||||Here is some additional information on my problem....it tells the whole story if someone cares to wade through it.<P>I have one problem with my 86GT that is driving me crazy. It seems to be in the computer???? I can drive the car and everything will be fine for several miles then as the car heats up the idle will start going up and down, then the car will die and not re-start. I can let it sit for five minutes and it will then re-start. All the time I am trying to start it I can tell the fuel pump is coming on but there is no fire from the coil.<P>I have rebuilt the motor (800 miles ago). At that time I replacing the 02 sensor, IAC, TPS, coolant temp sensor, MAP, EGR electric vacuum solenoid, Fuel pump & filter, Distributor & coil, Wires and had the Injectors cleaned and calibrated. I can not remember if I replaced the MAT or the VSS. The EGR valve is O.K., it works since I replaced the EGR electric vacuum solenoid and the tube going from the EGR to the air intake is O.K. also, I took it off and checked it by plugging it off and pulling a vacuum on the tube, no cracks. <P>I saw some notes about a Battery Voltage Correction Mode, I have a new battery…BUT…have placed it in the front compartment and connected the battery with 4 gage wire just like the orig. hookup. This could be a mistake, maybe I should have used 2 gage, I do not know if this could have any effect on the way the car runs but thought I would tell you everything.<P>Again, the car will run like a champ for several miles then as the car heats up the idle will start going up and down, then the car will die and not re-start, I will wait for five to ten minutes and it will then restart.<P>My son is in auto tech in high school, he hooked the computer up on a hand held device and it showed that the computer was putting the car through a lean/rich/lean/rich state. At the time he did not think anything about it till I started talking to him about the computer and how it functioned. Does this mean anything?<P>I REALLY NEED HELP WITH THIS ONE.<P>John Yokley<BR>800-877-6484 watts<BR>281-233-5713 work direct<BR>281-360-3681 home<BR>281-844-3160 portable<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||dogtired||01-13-2000||05:58 PM||||I think getting it up to temperature is the key to your problem???<BR>Ignition Module and Coil are very tempermental when it comes to heat.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>On a test bench they will check OK but in the hostile environment of the engine compartment it gets questionable.?????<BR>My guess is the ignition module, even though you have a fresh rebuild on the dist??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>I wouldn't purchase a NEW computer, I would ask here first?? If that is the direction you decide to go?? (Sorry I don't have any  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )||||reg||6
Z||000004||DRH||01-13-2000||06:07 PM||||5 minutes doesn't really sound like enough time for anything in the engine compartment to cool significantly. <P>Once it restarts, how long until it starts doing it again? <P>Has it done this since the rebuild or is this "new"?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||01-13-2000||06:18 PM||||the lean/rich flag is suposed to constantly change. If it doesn't then worry about it.<P>pull of the tach filter and see if it stops. if it doesn't try getting the rebuilt dist reploaced under warrantee. I'm assuming the dist came with a module and pickup.....||||reg||1
Z||000006||cmyokley||01-14-2000||11:45 AM||||dogtired, it is a rebuilt dist. and last week in an effort to fix this I replaced the module with a GM, still the same prob.<P>DHR, I purchased the car and never drove it before I rebuilt the motor and described. I have never driven it further than the house after it stalled the first time to see if it would stall again. Once is enough in one trip to work or home for me.<P>theorge, are you thinking it could be the dist? as described to DHR I have replaced the module in the rebuilt dist with a GM and no luck.<P>THANKS FOR THE HELP ALL...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||01-14-2000||09:17 PM||||Try this, get a dryer or heat gun. Gain access to your computer without removing it. Start the engine and with the heat gun apply heat to the computer but don't overdo it. If the problem occurs when you heat the computer, it is defective. Try this with your ignition module also.||||reg||1
